[Music]  in summer 2018 Secretary of Education  Betsy DeVos announced new guidelines on  a provision of the federal student loan  program known as borrower defense to  repayment devos fix a bizarre piece of  Obama era guidance which allowed the  Secretary of Education to grant  across-the-board loan forgiveness for  all borrowers in a program even to those  who could not show any evidence of harm  predictably divorces move was met with  the usual hysteria but these critiques  were both inaccurate and unfair after  all the whole point is that it's not  clear that all borrowers seeking loan  forgiveness actually have been to  frontal and since the Obama rules made  no meaningful effort to distinguish  between accidental misinformation and  deliberate fraud colleges were about to  become pinatas for target hungry lawyers  with taxpayers stuck footing the bill  the voss got this one right the new  rules make more sense for colleges tax  payers and students willing to repay  their debts how do you think we should  best balance the needs of student  borrowers and taxpayers let us know in  your comments also let us know what  other topics you'd like our scholars to  cover in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE  and subscribe for more research and  videos from AEI

